notes:
VM: the Function constructor assembles `(function anonymous(P
) {
body
})` (src/Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript/JsRealm.Dynamic.cs:159-187) and evaluates it once as a script through the provider (JsEngine.Eval.cs:121; a refusal becomes the SyntaxError at :135), so the wide front end's refusal of the assembled source is the only check (JsCompiler.cs:835, :863, :899) and vm_code is that source's own code. VM partial, by reading: P is never parsed alone, so a parameter text that is valid only inside the assembled source - the specification's own example, new Function("/*", "*/ ) {") - is accepted; no test262 test has it. A parameter text that fails alone and assembled, as the sample's `-->` does, is refused. JS: CreateDynamicFunction compiles the parameters in an empty function shell (JSFunction.cs:1353) before the body (:1354) and the whole (:1356), each through the full compile; a failure is the compile's SyntaxError. Slice: a call is a construct, refused by manifest.

VM: the Function constructor assembles `(function anonymous(P
) {
body
})` (src/Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript/JsRealm.Dynamic.cs:159-187) and evaluates it once as a script through the provider (JsEngine.Eval.cs:121; a refusal becomes the SyntaxError at :135), so the wide front end's refusal of the assembled source is the only check (JsCompiler.cs:835, :863, :899) and vm_code is that source's own code. VM partial, by reading: the body is never parsed alone, so a body that closes the function and opens another (body `}); (function () {`) assembles into a valid script and is accepted, answering the second function. A body that fails alone and assembled, as the sample's strict `with` does, is refused. JS: the body is compiled in an empty-parameter shell (JSFunction.cs:1354). Slice: a call is a construct, refused by manifest.

VM: the Function constructor assembles `(function anonymous(P
) {
body
})` (src/Broiler.VM.Profile.JavaScript/JsRealm.Dynamic.cs:159-187) and evaluates it once as a script through the provider (JsEngine.Eval.cs:121; a refusal becomes the SyntaxError at :135), so the wide front end's refusal of the assembled source is the only check (JsCompiler.cs:835, :863, :899) and vm_code is that source's own code. Every early error that spans parameters and body (a "use strict" body with duplicate or non-simple parameters, a parameter the body declares lexically) is the assembled script's refusal under its own rule's code. JS: the whole assembled source is compiled after the two parts (JSFunction.cs:1356). Slice: a call is a construct, refused by manifest.
